[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2558119363","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100694#issuecomment-2558119363","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100694","id":2558119363,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Yec3D","user":{"login":"hpvb","id":2591099,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1OTEwOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2591099?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb","html_url":"https://github.com/hpvb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-21T13:13:35Z","updated_at":"2024-12-21T13:15:40Z","body":"Very impressive work! That took quite some sleuthing.\r\n\r\nI wonder, however, of instead we should delete `operator&` from all of our CoWing types (Vector, String, etc), reason being that by taking a pointer to the container you circumvent CoW, which is what, in my mind, lies at the root of this. \r\n\r\nI think with a CoW datatype taking a pointer to it should be an error, because you should never be storing a reference to the container, you should always take a copy and rely on CoW to make it safe.\r\n\r\nIf a piece of code can't do that, then it shouldn't be using CoW to begin with. Especially now with the move operators, I feel that if you need to do processing on a CoW type to later pass it on, it is only marginally more expensive to just create a LocalVector to then later move it to a Vector for passing on by using `operator Vector<T>`.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2558119363/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2558160540","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100694#issuecomment-2558160540","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100694","id":2558160540,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Yem6c","user":{"login":"hpvb","id":2591099,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1OTEwOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2591099?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb","html_url":"https://github.com/hpvb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-21T16:03:59Z","updated_at":"2024-12-21T16:04:22Z","body":"I have changed my mind a little bit, I think that what I wrote above is true, it is also kind of off topic. \r\n\r\nWhen refcount == 0, the only valid state for ptr() is nullptr. Anything else would be a violation of the contract.\r\n\r\nEDIT: that is to say you are right. :)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https:/